        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Notre-Dame de Paris</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1163 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Begun by Maurice de Sully, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, and continued under Eudes de Sully by master builders whose names have been lost, then by Jean de Chelles, Pierre de Montreuil and later masters; restored in the 19th century by Jean-Baptiste Lassus and Eugène Viollet-le-Duc</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">A Gothic cathedral and basilica with a choir, nave, transepts, chapels and two west towers 69 metres high, using rib vaults, flying buttresses, three rose windows and richly sculpted portals</span></div>
